   "etymology": "From Proto-Albanian *báruka, from Proto-Indo-European *bʰor-uko-, from *bʰer- (“to carry”). Compare Messapic βάρυκα (báruka). A doublet of bie, barrë, and barrë.\nAnother reconstruction is Proto-Albanian *bárkʷa-, from earlier *bʰórkʷu- \"belly\", from a PIE *bʰorkʷó-, from *bʰer- (“to carry”).",
